<section class="sec" id="faq" style="background:#fff">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">FAQ</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">The questions people actually <span class="serif">ask.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">If yours isn't here, a counsellor answers it on a 20-minute call.</p>
<div class="faq-wrap">
<div class="acc reveal">
<details open=""><summary>Do I need supply-chain experience to learn SAP MM? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">No, though it helps. The course teaches procurement from first principles, and stores, purchase and logistics professionals find their floor experience becomes a consulting advantage rather than a prerequisite.</div></details>
<details><summary>What exactly will I learn in SAP MM? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">The complete procure-to-pay cycle: master data, purchasing, release strategies, inventory movements, invoice verification, OBYC account determination, special procurement like subcontracting and consignment, MRP basics, and S/4HANA Fiori procurement.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is the FI-MM integration really that important? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">It is the interview. GR/IR, OBYC and reconciling procurement to the ledger are where candidates fail and where projects break. We dedicate a full module plus a capstone to exactly this.</div></details>
<details><summary>Which certification does this course prepare me for? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">C_TS452, the SAP Certified Associate for S/4HANA Sourcing and Procurement, with two full mock exams. The exam is booked through SAP and charged separately.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is the starting salary for an SAP MM consultant? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Freshers typically start between Rs 4 and 6.5 lakh. With an implementation cycle behind you, Rs 7 to 12 lakh is common, and Gulf logistics roles pay substantially more.</div></details>
<details><summary>SAP MM or SAP FICO: which should I pick? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">FICO suits finance and accounting minds; MM suits operations, purchasing and supply-chain thinkers. Both ride the same S/4HANA migration wave. A counsellor maps your background honestly to the better fit.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is it online or classroom, and is Malayalam support available? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both. In-person batches in Trivandrum, Kochi and Bengaluru, plus live online batches across Kerala, the GCC and beyond. Sessions are in clear English with Malayalam support.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you guarantee a job after the course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">No, and we will not pretend otherwise. We provide structured placement support and real introductions across 400+ partners, with support continuing six months after you finish.</div></details>
